e-secops-concepts walkthrough log — 2026-10-10
Worked-case lesson: no command line by design (brief §6).
The "run" is the SoD matrix + privilege review + zero-trust gap assessment authored
and self-reviewed in-session against NIST SP 800-207 (tenets: no implicit trust by
network location/ownership; per-session access; dynamic policy; monitor everything)
and the CISA Zero Trust Maturity Model v2.0 pillar structure.

Scope: fictional Halcyon Health (240 staff, regional clinic network). Two scopes:
billing-system SoD and IT-estate privilege/zero-trust.
Artifacts authored (all fictional, labeled):
  - SoD matrix (billing): 6 duties × roles; toxic combinations marked (office
    manager creates vendors + approves payments; clerks submit + approve under
    undocumented threshold); separations restored or compensating controls
    recorded (DBA backup duties → witnessed restores + session recording).
  - Privilege review: 15 standing domain admins → 4 standing (justified,
    session-recorded) + 11 just-in-time (per-task request, second-person
    approval, auto-expiry); help-desk reset path checked against weaker-path rule.
  - Zero-trust gap assessment: 4 implicit-trust findings mapped to ZTMM pillars
    (identity: 2 legacy apps off SSO; devices: no posture check pre-VPN;
    networks: flat clinical net; data: no per-session policy on patient DB);
    roadmap ordered identity-first, each item with owner + quarter.

